---
import CaseStudy from '../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import architecture from '../assets/images/soc-architecture.png';
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Cloud-Native SOC Platform"
  subtitle="Multi-Tenant SIEM / EDR / IDS Infrastructure on Kubernetes"
  description="Case study: a cloud-native, open-source SOC platform on a three-node k3s cluster — Wazuh, OpenSearch, Suricata, Zeek, TheHive, and Cortex, provisioned with Terraform and Ansible."
  eyebrow="Case study — Graduation thesis (PFE)"
  tags={['k3s', 'Wazuh', 'OpenSearch', 'Suricata', 'Zeek', 'TheHive', 'Cortex', 'Proxmox VE', 'Terraform', 'Ansible']}
  meta={[
    { label: 'Type', value: 'Final-year thesis (PFE)' },
    { label: 'Context', value: 'Internship, Flexos Tunisie' },
    { label: 'Period', value: 'Dec 2025 – Jun 2026' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'Completed' },
  ]}
>
  <!-- Overview -->
  <section>
    <p class="section-label">Overview</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">What was built and why</h2>
    <div class="text-text-muted space-y-4 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        This project was the final-year engineering thesis (PFE) completed during an internship at Flexos Tunisie.
        The goal was to design and deploy a production-grade, open-source security operations platform capable of
        supporting multi-tenant threat detection, log aggregation, network analysis, and incident case management —
        without relying on commercial SaaS solutions.
      </p>
      <p>
        The platform was intended to demonstrate that a fully functional SOC stack could be built using mature
        open-source tools, orchestrated on Kubernetes, and deployed on commodity hardware — making it replicable
        for organizations of varying sizes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-bg-600" />

  <!-- Architecture -->
  <section>
    <p class="section-label">Architecture</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">System design and component roles</h2>

    <div class="text-text-muted space-y-4 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      <p>
        The platform runs on a three-node k3s Kubernetes cluster deployed on Proxmox VE bare-metal hypervisors.
        Network stability was enforced via Netplan static IP configuration to avoid DHCP-induced failures.
        Persistent storage is managed via local-path provisioner, with key configuration stored in Kubernetes
        ConfigMaps and Secrets.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Architecture diagram -->
    <div class="mb-10">
      <Figure
        src={architecture}
        alt="Architecture diagram of a cloud-native open-source SOC platform with Kubernetes, Wazuh, OpenSearch, Suricata, Zeek, TheHive, Cortex, Terraform, Ansible, and Proxmox."
        caption="End-to-end architecture of the cloud-native SOC platform, including data sources, detection stack, SIEM, incident response, automation, and infrastructure layers."
      />
    </div>

    <!-- Component table -->
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-bg-700">
            <th class="text-left font-mono text-xs text-text-dim uppercase tracking-widest py-3 pr-8">Component</th>
            <th class="text-left font-mono text-xs text-text-dim uppercase tracking-widest py-3 pr-8">Role</th>
            <th class="text-left font-mono text-xs text-text-dim uppercase tracking-widest py-3">Technology</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-text-muted">
          {[
            ['EDR / HIDS', 'Host-based threat detection, file integrity monitoring, log collection', 'Wazuh'],
            ['SIEM', 'Log aggregation, search, security analytics dashboards', 'OpenSearch + Security Analytics'],
            ['Network IDS', 'Packet inspection and network protocol analysis', 'Suricata + Zeek'],
            ['SOAR / Case Mgmt', 'Alert triage, case creation, workflow automation', 'TheHive + Cortex'],
            ['Infrastructure', 'Multi-node Kubernetes orchestration', 'k3s on Proxmox VE'],
            ['IaC & Config', 'Reproducible provisioning and configuration management', 'Terraform + Ansible'],
          ].map(([role, desc, tech]) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-bg-800 hover:bg-bg-700/30 transition-colors">
              <td class="py-3 pr-8 text-text-primary font-medium">{role}</td>
              <td class="py-3 pr-8">{desc}</td>
              <td class="py-3 font-mono text-xs text-accent-cyan">{tech}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-bg-600" />

  <!-- Detection Rules -->
  <section>
    <p class="section-label">Detection Engineering</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Custom MITRE ATT&CK–mapped rules</h2>
    <div class="text-text-muted space-y-4 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      <p>
        Four custom detection rules were written and validated against real attack simulations.
        Rules are persisted via a dedicated <code class="code-inline">wazuh-custom-rules</code> ConfigMap
        to survive pod restarts, avoiding the common pitfall of rules stored only in ephemeral PVC paths.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      {[
        { id: '100100', technique: 'T1110.001', name: 'SSH Brute Force Detection', level: '10', status: 'Validated' },
        { id: '100101', technique: 'T1548.003', name: 'Privilege Escalation via sudo', level: '14', status: 'Validated' },
        { id: '100102', technique: 'T1046', name: 'Suricata Network Recon Detection', level: '10', status: 'Validated' },
        { id: '100103', technique: 'T1087.001', name: 'Windows Account Discovery', level: '10', status: 'Validated' },
      ].map((rule) => (
        <div class="card-base border border-bg-600">
          <div class="flex items-start justify-between mb-2">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent-cyan">Rule {rule.id}</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-[10px] text-accent-green border border-accent-green/30 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">{rule.status}</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-text-primary text-sm font-medium mb-1">{rule.name}</p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-text-dim">MITRE: {rule.technique}</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-text-dim">Level: {rule.level}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-bg-600" />

  <!-- Results -->
  <section>
    <p class="section-label">Results</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">Validated in the lab scenario</h2>
    <div class="card-base border border-accent-green/20 bg-accent-green/5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center gap-4 mb-4">
      <div class="font-display text-4xl text-accent-green shrink-0">&lt;4s</div>
      <p class="text-text-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">
        End-to-end SSH brute-force detection and automated containment — from Suricata/Wazuh alert
        to response action — completed in under 4 seconds in the project's controlled lab scenario.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-text-dim">
      This result reflects the validated lab scenario only; it has not been measured at production
      scale or under production network conditions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-bg-600" />

  <!-- Challenges -->
  <section>
    <p class="section-label">Challenges & Solutions</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary mb-4">What went wrong, and how it was fixed</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
      {[
        {
          problem: 'DHCP-induced IP change on worker node',
          solution: 'Migrated all nodes to static IPs via Netplan configuration. Added this as a prerequisite step in the deployment runbook.',
        },
        {
          problem: 'Wazuh master ConfigMap wiped after network incident',
          solution: 'Restored ConfigMap from version-controlled YAML. Established GitOps discipline for all ConfigMap state.',
        },
        {
          problem: 'Port 1514 (agent ingress) drops after pod restarts',
          solution: 'Identified root cause as stale svclb-wazuh-workers pods in kube-system. Fix: delete and allow them to respawn after each Wazuh restart.',
        },
        {
          problem: 'Custom detection rules lost on pod restart',
          solution: 'Moved rules from PVC to a dedicated wazuh-custom-rules ConfigMap, mounted read-only. Rules now persist and are version-controlled.',
        },
        {
          problem: 'TheHive case flood (843 cases from noise)',
          solution: 'Raised Wazuh–TheHive integration threshold from level 10 to level 12, eliminating low-signal alerts while preserving high-severity escalations.',
        },
      ].map((item) => (
        <div class="card-base border border-bg-600">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-red-400/60 mt-1 shrink-0">✕</span>
            <div>
              <p class="text-text-muted text-sm mb-2"><span class="text-text-primary font-medium">Problem:</span> {item.problem}</p>
              <p class="text-text-muted text-sm"><span class="text-accent-green font-medium">Solution:</span> {item.solution}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr class="border-bg-600" />

  <!-- Key takeaways -->
  <section>
    <p class="section-label">Takeaways</p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl text-text-primary mb-6">What this project demonstrated</h2>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      {[
        'End-to-end ownership of a cloud-native security infrastructure from design to deployment',
        'Practical Kubernetes operations: debugging, networking, persistence, and config management',
        'Detection engineering grounded in real threat frameworks (MITRE ATT&CK)',
        'Infrastructure-as-code discipline using Terraform and Ansible for reproducible deployments',
        'Incident management pipeline design from raw alert to enriched case in TheHive',
        'Resilience engineering: identifying failure modes and building durable operational fixes',
      ].map((point) => (
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3 card-base border border-bg-600">
          <span class="text-accent-cyan mt-0.5 shrink-0">▸</span>
          <p class="text-text-muted text-sm">{point}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</CaseStudy>
